	The X support seem OK, if spartan, to me. Look alot like the Mac and
	Amiga setups. Looks like their window abstraction layer is working
	good across multiple windowing systems.

	The problem lies in that they didn't provide and Imakefile for the
	X support and therefore the X support won't compile without much
	grief and nashing of teeth for those whose systems require the linker
	lines from hell in order to link in X support. Imakefiles normally
	take care of this. The Rat Shit 6000 setup and X11R4 under AmigaUNIX
	are both in the "link lines from hell" catagory unfortunately. The
	SVR4 X11R5 setup only requires an additional -L/usr/X11R5/lib on
	most systems to catch all the needed libs. You also usually need to
	at a -I/usr/X11R5/include to the compiler lines to pick up the
	right X header files.

	Now, if only the AmigaDOS version supported sound like the Mac
	and X86 UNIX versions do...

